From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:17:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: decoder: Do not bound the sink caps below by the
 smallest coded size

gst_v4l2_decoder_probe_sink_caps() put the STEPWISE minimum that
VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES reports into the sink pad template as the lower
bound of width and height. That minimum is a coded frame size (cedrus
reports 16x16, Hantro 48x48), while the caps carry the display size: a
picture smaller than one macroblock is coded at the minimum size and
decodes fine, the driver rounds the format up. With the bound, a 15x15,
8x8 or 1x1 JPEG (or an 8x8 H.264 stream) is refused by the caps and
autopluggers fall back to a software decoder for exactly the pictures
the hardware handles trivially.

Keep only the maximum, for the same reason the step is already left out.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
index a634530..98ee880 100644
--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
@@ -480,13 +480,16 @@ gst_v4l2_decoder_probe_sink_caps (GstV4l2Decoder * self, guint32 pix_fmt,
     gst_caps_unref (caps);
     caps = sized_caps;
   } else {
-    /* For STEPWISE, the step is not expressed in the caps, since the caps
-     * carry the display size, which may not be aligned to the step */
+    /* For STEPWISE, neither the step nor the minimum is expressed in the
+     * caps: both constrain the coded frame size, while the caps carry the
+     * display size, which need not be aligned to the step and may be smaller
+     * than the smallest coded size (the driver rounds the format up). Only
+     * the maximum excludes a decoder. */
     caps = gst_caps_make_writable (caps);
-    gst_v4l2_decoder_set_size_range (caps, "width", size.stepwise.min_width,
+    gst_v4l2_decoder_set_size_range (caps, "width", 1,
         size.stepwise.max_width);
-    gst_v4l2_decoder_set_size_range (caps, "height",
-        size.stepwise.min_height, size.stepwise.max_height);
+    gst_v4l2_decoder_set_size_range (caps, "height", 1,
+        size.stepwise.max_height);
   }
 
   GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (self, "Probed sink caps: %" GST_PTR_FORMAT, caps);
-- 
